    "result_text": "There's only one test class, and it passes. The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the string membership tier with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133), touching two files:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Replaced the `membershipTier` (string) response property with `membershipLevel` (integer, min 1, max 3), removing `membershipTier` from the response.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Replaced the single `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto` with the new level rule:\n   `Math.min(3, 1 + (email present ? 1 : 0) + (namesakeCount == 0 ? 1 : 0))` \u2014 starts at 1, +1 for email, +1 for zero namesakes, capped at 3.\n\n**On the audit line:** the create audit line (`OwnerRestControllerV1:134`) logs `id/customerCode/registrationDate` and never recorded the tier, so nothing there needed changing \u2014 the tier was only ever derived in the mapper.\n\n**Structural impact:** I kept the change to exactly one modified function (`toOwnerDto`'s mapping annotation \u2014 a single line) plus the schema. I deliberately kept the logic inline rather than extracting a new helper class: adding a file would have multiplied the total cost by a third touched file, which outweighs the small WMC of the mapper interface. Net: 1 function changed, 2 files touched.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreNumericLevel` (email + namesakeCount 0 \u2192 level 3) and the full build pass green.",
